{
  "slug": "imperativo",
  "number": 21,
  "part": 5,
  "level": "A2",
  "title": "The imperative",
  "tagline": "Giving orders, advice and instructions, positive and negative.",
  "goal": "Form the imperative of any verb, know the four irregular ones, make it negative and place the pronouns.",
  "minutes": 11,
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "formas",
      "title": "Three persons, no subject",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "English has one imperative («Speak!»). French has **three**: *tu* (one person you know well), *vous* (several people, or polite) and *nous* (= «let's»). Take the **present** tense [[5]] and drop the subject."
        },
        {
          "type": "conjugation",
          "persons": ["(tu)", "(nous)", "(vous)"],
          "verbs": [
            { "verb": "parler", "meaning": "to speak", "forms": ["parl{e} !", "parl{ons} !", "parl{ez} !"] },
            { "verb": "finir", "meaning": "to finish", "forms": ["fin{is} !", "finiss{ons} !", "finiss{ez} !"] },
            { "verb": "prendre", "meaning": "to take", "forms": ["prend{s} !", "pren{ons} !", "pren{ez} !"] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "warning",
          "title": "-er verbs lose their s",
          "text": "*tu parles* → *{Parle} !* · *tu manges* → *{Mange} !* · *tu vas* → *{Va} !* Same with *ouvrir* and *offrir*: *{Ouvre} la porte !*"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The s comes back before *y* and *en* [[16]], for the sound: *{Vas-y} ! · Parles-en à ton père.*"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "irregulares",
      "title": "The four irregular ones",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": ["Verb", "tu", "nous", "vous"],
          "rows": [
            ["*être*", "*sois*", "*soyons*", "*soyez*"],
            ["*avoir*", "*aie*", "*ayons*", "*ayez*"],
            ["*savoir*", "*sache*", "*sachons*", "*sachez*"],
            ["*vouloir*", "—", "—", "*veuillez*"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "examples",
          "items": [
            { "fr": "{Sois} patient.", "tr": "Be patient." },
            { "fr": "N'{aie} pas peur !", "tr": "Don't be afraid!", "note": "French «has» fear: avoir peur" },
            { "fr": "{Veuillez} patienter.", "tr": "Please wait.", "note": "very formal: announcements, emails" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "negativo",
      "title": "Negative orders",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "No «don't» to add: just wrap the verb in *ne… pas* [[12]], as in any other sentence."
        },
        {
          "type": "examples",
          "items": [
            { "fr": "Parle ! → {Ne} parle {pas} !", "tr": "Speak! → Don't speak!" },
            { "fr": "Touchez ça ! → {Ne} touchez {pas} ça !", "tr": "Touch that! → Don't touch that!" },
            { "fr": "Oublie ! → {N'}oublie {pas} !", "tr": "Forget! → Don't forget!" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pronombres",
      "title": "Where the pronouns go",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In a **positive** order, the pronoun goes **after** the verb, as in English («Take it!»), joined with a hyphen. In a **negative** order it goes back **in front** [[15]]."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": ["Positive", "Negative"],
          "rows": [
            ["*Prends{-le} !* (Take it!)", "*Ne {le} prends pas !*"],
            ["*Dis{-lui} la vérité.* (Tell him / her)", "*Ne {lui} dis pas.*"],
            ["*Regarde{-moi} !* (Look at me!)", "*Ne {me} regarde pas !*"],
            ["*Lève{-toi} !* (Get up!)", "*Ne {te} lève pas !*"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "warning",
          "title": "Me and te become moi and toi",
          "text": "Only in positive orders, at the end: *Assieds{-toi}. Excusez{-moi}.* That's why reflexive verbs [[17]] give *Lève-toi*, *Dépêchez-vous* (Hurry up)."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exercises": [
